      "name": "Neeraj Lilani",
      "created_at": "2025-08-26T15:09:32.611Z",
      "cooked": "<p><strong>Problem statement:</strong><br>\nSearching Sales Invoices (and other DocTypes) is too strict: entering only the numeric portion (e.g., 10234) or missing a hyphen in an ID (INV-10234 vs INV10234) returns no results, and common series prefixes must be typed exactly. This slows down daily work and causes “no results” confusion when users only remember the significant number.</p>\n<p><strong>Proposed feature:</strong></p>\n<pre><code>Support tolerant matching in link fields and list search: ignore hyphens/whitespace and allow matching on the numeric segment of names.\n\nAdd prefix-aware logic: when a naming series is configured (e.g., INV-YYYY-), allow searching by the unique trailing portion without typing the series.\n\nEnable fuzzy/contains match for IDs by default (or via a system setting) and rank exact/starts-with matches higher to preserve precision for power users.\n\nExtend to global search and link field autocomplete, with admin controls to tune strictness per DocType.\n</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Benefits/use cases:</strong></p>\n<pre><code>Faster retrieval in accounting and sales where staff commonly recall only the trailing number.\n\nFewer “no result” dead ends, better onboarding, and alignment with how users search in other ERPs and POS tools.\n</code></pre>",
